## 9. Interview Questions

**Q1. What is concatenation of an array?**

Combining an array with itself in this problem.

**Q2. Why do we multiply the length by 2?**

Because the new array contains two copies of the original array.

**Q3. Why do we use `i + nums.length`?**

To access the corresponding index in the second half.

**Q4. What does `ans[i] = nums[i]` do?**

Copies an element from the original array into the first half.

**Q5. What is the time complexity?**

O(n).

**Q6. Can we solve this using one loop?**

Yes. Each iteration copies one element into two positions.

